  "rendered": "To calculate the diffusion time, we need to use the equation:\n\nt = l^2 / D\n\nwhere t is the diffusion time, l is the diffusion length (which is the thickness of the coating, 10 nm in this case), and D is the diffusivity of the lithium ion in the coating material.\n\nFrom Table 5, we can see that the diffusivity of ZrO2 is 1.7 × 10^−18 cm^2/s.\n\nFirst, we need to convert the thickness of the coating from nanometers to centimeters:\n\n10 nm = 10 × 10^−7 cm\n\nNow we can plug in the values:\n\nt = (10 × 10^−7 cm)^2 / (1.7 × 10^−18 cm^2/s)\n\nt = 10^−14 cm^2 / 1.7 × 10^−18 cm^2/s\n\nt = 5.88 × 10^3 s\n\nTherefore, it would take approximately 5880 seconds, or about 1.63 hours, for a lithium ion to cross a 10 nm ZrO2 coating.",
